      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": " Presented in excellent condition throughout, this spacious four-bedroom detached bungalow occupies a generous site of approximately 0.54 acres in a peaceful countryside setting just moments from the picturesque heritage village of Multyfarnham. Offering comfortable family living with endless potential, this attractive home combines generous accommodation with well-maintained gardens, while enjoying rural living and modern convenience, just off the N4 and only a short drive from Mullingar.\n\nThe accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall leading to a bright and spacious living room featuring a marble fireplace with cast iron inset solid fuel stove. An impressive open-plan kitchen and dining area, fitted with an extensive range of units and complemented by a large solid fuel stove. There are four well-proportioned bedrooms, all finished with laminate flooring, while the family bathroom is fitted with a modern suite including a fully tiled shower cubicle.\n\nExternally, the property is surrounded by mature lawns offering excellent privacy and plenty of outdoor space for families to enjoy. A substantial detached garage provides valuable storage or workshop space, while the large side entrance and extensive driveway offer ample off-street parking.\n\nIdeally positioned within walking distance of Multyfarnham Village, residents can enjoy an excellent range of local amenities including shops, cafés, pubs, schools, sporting facilities and two award-winning restaurants. The village is renowned for its strong sense of community, historic friary and beautiful natural surroundings. Ballinafid Lake and the crystal-clear waters of Lough Owel are just moments away, offering fishing, swimming, kayaking, boating and scenic lakeside walks, while Gaine Park, Abbey Blooms Botanical Gardens and a selection of heritage trails provide further recreational opportunities. Convenient access to the N4 ensures excellent connectivity to Mullingar, just 7km away, and beyond.\n\nOffering spacious accommodation, a superb location and a generous site in one of Westmeath's most desirable villages, this is an outstanding opportunity to acquire a wonderful family home within Ireland's Hidden Heartlands. Viewing is highly recommended.\n\nAccommodation\nEntrance Hall 1.8m x 4.18m (5'11\" x 13'9\"): \nTiled floor.\n\nHallway 1.2m x 5.77m (3'11\" x 18'11\"): \nHotpress.\n\nLiving Room 4.84m x 3.41m (15'11\" x 11'2\"): Laminate flooring, marble fireplace with cast iron inset solid fuel stove.\n\nKitchen/Dining Area \n6.99m x 4.73m (22'11\" x 15'6\"): \nImpressive fully fitted kitchen, tiled floor, wall tiling, large solid fuel stove, hotpress.\n\nBedroom One 4.74m x 2.91m (15'7\" x 9'7\"): \nLaminate floor.\n\nBedroom Two 3.87m x 2.83m (12'8\" x 9'3\"): \nLaminate floor, coving.\n\nBedroom Three 3.46m x 2.91m (11'4\" x 9'7\"): \nLaminate floor, coving.\n\nBedroom Four 3.91m x 4.26m (12'10\" x 14'): \nLaminate floor, coving.\n\nBathroom 2.1m x 2.11m (6'11\" x 6'11\"): \nFully tiled shower cubicle with electric shower, WC, wash hand basin, wall tiling, tiled floor.\n\nDetached Garage \n8.77m x 4.84m (28'9\" x 15'11\"): \n\nSpecial Features & Services\n•OFCH\n•PVC Double glazed windows and doors\n•Renovated property\n•Excellent finish\n•Mature lawns\n•Detached garage\n•Short walk into Multyfarnham Village\n•Close to N4\n•Close to all amenities\n•Close to Multyfarnham Friary\n•Close to local GAA pitch & Playground\n•Spacious property\n•Ideal for First Time Buyer\n•Ample parking\n•Large side entrance\n•Close to local schools\n•Picturesque heritage village just 15 minutes from Mullingar. \n•Convenient to the N4 \n•Strong sense of community with an active GAA club and year-round local events. \n•Heritage trails nearby\n•Close to Lough Owel, renowned for its crystal-clear waters, scenic walks, wildlife and fishing. \n•Gaine Park features a modern playground, looped walking trail, green spaces and picnic areas, ideal for families. \n•Excellent primary education at St. Cremin's National School, with the well-regarded Wilson's Hospital School nearby. \n•Community centre, nursing home and sporting facilities all within the village. \n•Nearby Abbey Blooms Botanical Gardens offers beautifully landscaped gardens, a café and garden centre. \n•Located in Ireland's Hidden Heartlands\n\nIncluded\n•Curtains\n•Blinds\n•Light fittings\n•Fixtures & fittings\n\nBER \nBER C, \nBER No. 109200253\n\n"
      },
